sub=dict(action='research',rationale='Register a usable initial two-core-path map and retain sourced path discrepancies without presuming a defect or manufacturing an obligation.',sources=sources,map_path='map.json',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['s-config-switch','s-read-release','s-election','s-node-contract','s-read-contract','s-confchange','s-joint','s-node-loop','s-timers'],answered='Traced election and replication quorum consumers, configuration application, recovery, read-index tracking and application boundaries. Commit establishment is path-specific: append response invokes postponed-read release; switchToConfig commitment does not. The campaign guard against unapplied committed configuration and ReadIndex loss/retry contract are important contrary evidence for a liveness interpretation. Retained a separate auto-leave/transfer retry lead. Pending pre-gate reads survive reset but release reruns the current term gate and safe-mode quorum acquisition, so persistence of the queue alone does not establish stale-authority consumption.',remaining=['Investigate whether a legal application/election history reaches configuration-driven first-current-term commitment with a postponed read, and whether an applicable bounded completion duty exists.','Inspect automatic joint exit contract and transfer-abort retry callers; compare this source lead with the unresolved persistence-order contract before committing to a costly execution.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The map supports focused investigation while preserving local discrepancies and contrary evidence. Smaller contract and producer-history work can distinguish unreachable or permitted pending behavior from a missed required effect.'))
open('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(sub,indent=2)+'\n')
